{
  "title": "Daily supplications of Rajab",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "Second: It is recommended to say the following supplicatory prayer that Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) used to say everyday in Rajab:\nخَابَ الْوَافِدُوْنَ عَلٰى غَيْرِكَ\nKHAABAL WAAFEDOONA A’LAA GHAYREKA\nThose who approach other than You are disappointed.\nوَ خَسِرَ الْمُتَعَرِّضُوْنَ اِلَّا لَكَ\nWA KHASERAL MOTA-A’RREZOONA ILLAA LAKA \nThose who try to gain the favour of other than You are losers;\nوَ ضَاعَ الْمُلِمُّوْنَ اِلَّا بِكَ\nWA ZAA-A’L MOLIMMOONA ILLAA BEKA \nthose who make other than You the goal of their journey perish;\nوَ اَجْدَبَ الْمُنْتَجِعُوْنَ اِلَّا مَنِ انْتَجَعَ فَضْلَكَ\nWA AJDABAL MUNTAJE-O’ONA ILLAA MANIN TAJA-A’ FAZLAKA \nand all except those who seek resort in Your grace face desolation\nبَابُكَ مَفْتُوْحٌ لِلرَّاغِبِيْنَ\nBAABOKA MAFTOOHUL LIR-RAAGHEBEENA \nYour door is open for the seekers\nوَ خَيْرُكَ مَبْذُوْلٌ لِلطَّالِبِيْنَ\nWA KHAYROKA MABZOOLUL LIT-TAALEBEENA \nand your boons are given to those who seek them,\nوَ فَضْلُكَ مُبَاحٌ لِلسَّاۤئِلِيْنَ\nWA FAZLOKA MOBAAHUN LIS-SAAA-ELEENA \nand Your grace is freely available to those who ask for it,\nوَ نَيْلُكَ مُتَاحٌ لِلْآمِلِيْنَ\nWA NAYLOKA MOTAAHUN LIL-AAMELEENA \nAccess to You is granted to those who hope for it!\nوَ رِزْقُكَ مَبْسُوْطٌ لِمَنْ عَصَاكَ\nWA RIZQOKA MABSOOTUN LEMAN A’SAAKA\nYour sustenance is extended for even those who disobey You.\nوَ حِلْمُكَ مُعْتَرِضٌ لِمَنْ نَاوَاكَ\nWA HILMOKA MO’TAREZOON LEMAN NAAWAAKA \nYour forbearance extends to those who antagonize You.\nعَادَتُكَ الْاِحْسَانُ اِلَى الْمُسِيْئِيْنَ\nA-A’DATOKAL EHSAANO ELAL MOSEE-EENA \nYour habit is to do favor to the wrongdoers\nوَ سَبِيْلُكَ الْاِبْقَاءُ عَلَى الْمُعْتَدِيْنَ\nWA SABEELOKAL IBQAAA-O A’LAL MO’TADEENA\nand Your way is to be benevolent to the transgressors.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ فَاهْدِنِي هُدَى الْمُهْتَدِيْنَ\nALLAAHUMMA FAHDENEE HODAL MOHTADEENA\nO Allah, so (lovingly) guide me with guidance enjoyed by the rightly-guided,\nوَ ارْزُقْنِي اجْتِهَادَ الْمُجْتَهِدِيْنَ\nWAR ZUQNEE IJTEHAADAL MUJTAHEDEENA\nand enable me to strive like the diligent,\nوَ لَا تَجْعَلْنِي مِنَ الْغَافِلِيْنَ الْمُبْعَدِيْنَ\nWA LAA TAJ-A’LNEE MENAL GHAAFELEENAL MUB-A’DEENA \ndo not place me with the negligent who are kept at a distance from You\nوَ اغْفِرْ لِيْ يَوْمَ الدِّينِ.\nWAGH-FIR LEE YAWMAD DEENE.\nand forgive me on the Day of Retribution.\nThird: In his book of al-Misbah, Shaykh al-Tusi mentions that al-Mu’alla ibn Khunays has reported Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) as saying, “In Rajab, you may say the following supplicatory prayer:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْ اَسْاَلُكَ صَبْرَ الشَّاكِرِيْنَ لَكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOKA SABRASH SHAAKEREENA LAKA\nO Allah, I implore You to grant me the patience of those who always thank You,\nوَ عَمَلَ الْخَاۤئِفِيْنَ مِنْكَ\nWA A’MALAL KHAAA-EFEENA MINKA \nthe efforts of those who fear You,\nوَ يَقِيْنَ الْعَابِدِيْنَ لَكَ\nWA YAQEENAL A’ABEDEENA LAKA \nand the conviction of those who worship You devoutly.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اَنْتَ الْعَلِيُّ الْعَظِيْمُ\nALLAAHUMMA ANTAL A’LIYYUL A’ZEEMO \nO Allah, You are the Most High, the All-Supreme,\nوَ اَنَا عَبْدُكَ الْبَاۤئِسُ الْفَقِيْرُ\nWA ANAA A’BDOKAL BAAA-ESUL FAQEERO \nand I am Your servant—the destitute and the needy.\nاَنْتَ الْغَنِيُّ الْحَمِيدُ\nANTAL GHANIYYUL HAMEEDO \nYou are the Self-Sufficient, the Praised,\nوَ اَنَا الْعَبْدُ الذَّلِيْلُ\nWA ANAA A’BDUZ ZALEELO \nand I am the abject and lowly servant.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَ اٰلِهٖ\nALLAAHUMMA SALE A’LAA MOHAMMADIN WA AALEHI \nO Allah, bless Muhammad and his Household\nوَ امْنُنْ بِغِنَاكَ عَلٰی فَقْرِيْ\nWAM-NUN BE-GHENAAKA A’LAA FAQREE\nand favour me with Your sufficiency upon my poverty, \nوَ بِحِلْمِكَ عَلٰى جَهْلِيْ\nWA BE-HILMEKA A’LAA JAHLEE \nand with Your forbearance upon my ignorance,\nوَ بِقُوَّتِكَ عَلٰى ضَعْفِيْ\nWA BE-QUWWATEKA A’LAA ZA’FEE\nand with Your strength on my weakness,\nيَا قَوِيُّ يَا عَزِيْزُ\nYAA QAWIYYO YAA A’ZEEZO\nO All-Strong, O Almighty.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى مُحَمَّدٍ وَ اٰلِهِ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADIN WA AALEHIL\nO Allah, bless Muhammad and his Household;\nالْاَوْصِيَاءِ الْمَرْضِيِّيْنَ\nAWSEYAAA-IL MARZIYYEENA \nthe Successors (of prophet hood) and the Pleased;\nوَ اكْفِنِيْ مَا اَهَمَّنِيْ مِنْ اَمْرِ الدُّنْيَا وَ الْآخِرَةِ\nWAK-FENEE MAA AHAMMANEE MIN AMRID DUNYAA WAL AAKHERATE \nand suffice me from whatever aggrieves me from the affairs pertaining to the world and the Hereafter.\nيَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ.\nYAA ARHAMAR RAAHEMEENA.\nO most Merciful of all those who show mercy!\nThe previously mentioned supplicatory prayer has been also mentioned by Sayyid Ibn Tawus al-Hasani in his book of Iqbal al-A’mal. According to the narration, this supplicatory prayer is the most comprehensive and it is advisable to repeat it any time.\nFourth: Shaykh al-Tusi has also mentioned that the following supplicatory prayer is advisedly repeated each day in Rajab:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ يَا ذَا الْمِنَنِ السَّابِغَةِ\nALLAAHUMMA YAA ZAL MENANIS SAABEGHATE\nO Allah, the Lord of the complete favors,\nوَ الْآلَاءِ الْوَازِعَةِ\nWAL AALAAIL WAAZE-A’TE\nthe utter bounties,\nوَ الرَّحْمَةِ الْوَاسِعَةِ\nWAR RAHMATIL WAASEA’TE,\nthe immense mercy,\nوَ الْقُدْرَةِ الْجَامِعَةِ\nWAL QUDRATIL JAAME-A’TE \nand all-encompassing power,\nوَ النِّعَمِ الْجَسِيْمَةِ\nWAN NEA’AMIL JASEEMATE\nand the immense blessings,\nوَ الْمَوَاهِبِ الْعَظِيْمَةِ\nWAL MAWAAHEBIL A’ZEEMATE \nand the great gifts,\nوَ الْاَيَادِي الْجَمِيْلَةِ\nWAL AYAADIL JAMEELATE \nand the elegant boons,\nوَ الْعَطَايَا الْجَزِيْلَةِ\nWAL A’TAAYAL JAZEELATE \nand plentiful rewards!\nيَا مَنْ لَا يُنْعَتُ بِتَمْثِيْلٍ\nYAA MAN LAA YUN-A’TO BE-TAMSEELIN\nO He Who cannot be described by any analogy, \nوَ لَا يُمَثَّلُ بِنَظِيْرٍ\nWA LAA YOMASSALO BE-NAZEERIN\nnor compared with any like,\nوَ لَا يُغْلَبُ بِظَهِيْرٍ\nWA LAA YUGHLABO BE-ZAHEERIN\nand nor overcome with the help of any supporter.\nيَا مَنْ خَلَقَ فَرَزَقَ\nYAA MAN KHALAQA FA-RAZAQA \nO He Who created and then granted sustenance,\nوَ اَلْهَمَ فَاَنْطَقَ\nWA ALHAMA FA-ANTAQA\nand inspired (them) and then endowed them with speech,\nوَ ابْتَدَعَ فَشَرَعَ\nWAB TADA-A’ FA-SHARA-A’, \nand originated (the creation) and then initiated it,\nوَ عَلَا فَارْتَفَعَ\nWA A’LAA FARTAFA-A’,\ntranscended it and then surmounted it,\nوَ قَدَّرَ فَاَحْسَنَ\nWA QADDARA FA-AHSANA, \nand determined it in an excellent form,\nوَ صَوَّرَ فَاَتْقَنَ\nWA SAWWARA FA-ATQANA, \nand then formed it in a perfect manner,\nوَ احْتَجَّ فَاَبْلَغَ\nWAH TAJJA FA-ABLAGHA, \nand advanced conclusive proofs,\nوَ اَنْعَمَ فَاَسْبَغَ\nWA AN-A’MA FA-ASBAGHA,\nand blessed abundantly,\nوَ اَعْطٰى فَاَجْزَلَ\nWA A-A’TAA FA-AJZALA, \nand rewarded plenteously,\nوَ مَنَحَ فَاَفْضَلَ\nWA MANAHA FA-AFZALA\nand conferred gracious gifts!\nيَا مَنْ سَمَا فِي الْعِزِّ\nYAA MAN SAMAA FIL-I’ZZE\nO He Who is so lofty in might \nفَفَاتَ نَوَاظِرَ الْاَبْصَارِ\nFA-FAATA NAWAAZERAL ABSAARE, \nso he eludes the gaze of the creatures' eyes,\nوَ دَنَا فِي اللُّطْفِ\nWA DANAA FIL LUTFE \nand so close in affection\nفَجَازَ هَوَاجِسَ الْاَفْكَارِ\nFA-JAAZA HAWAAJESAL AFKAARE \nso as to ascend all notions of thought!\nيَا مَنْ تَوَحَّدَ بِالْمُلْكِ\nYAA MAN TAWAHHADA BIL-MULKE\nO He Who is the sole sovereign of His dominion\nفَلَا نِدَّ لَهٗ فِىْ مَلَكُوْتِ سُلْطَانِهٖ\nFALAA NIDDA LAHU FEE MALAKOOTE SULTAANEHI \nthat no peer can ever be found for Him in the realms of His power\nوَ تَفَرَّدَ بِالْآلَاءِ وَ الْكِبْرِيَاءِ\nWA TAFARRADA BIL-AALAAA-E WAL-KIBREYAA-E \nand has been so matchless in bounties and supremacy\nفَلَا ضِدَّ لَهٗ فِیْ جَبَرُوْتِ شَاْنِهٖ\nFALAA ZIDDA LAHU FEE JABAROOTE SHAANEHI \nthat nothing can oppose Him in the omnipotence of His situation!\nيَا مَنْ حَارَتْ فِي كِبْرِيَاءِ هَيْبَتِهٖ دَقَاۤئِقُ لَطَاۤئِفِ الْاَوْهَامِ\nYAA MAN HAARATA FEE KIBREYAA-E HAYBATEHI DAQAAEQO LATAAEFIL AWHAAME \nO He the greatness of whose awe, bewilders the intricate subtleties of the imagination\nوَ انْحَسَرَتْ دُوْنَ اِدْرَاكِ عَظَمَتِهٖ خَطَاۤئِفُ اَبْصَارِ الْاَنَامِ\nWAN HASARAT DOONA IDRAAKE A’ZAMATEHI KHATAAEFO ABSAARIL ANAAME. \nand before Whose greatness are wearied the glances of the eyes of the worlds inhabitants!\nيَا مَنْ عَنَتِ الْوُجُوْهُ لِهَيْبَتِهٖ\nYAA MAN A’NATIL WOJOOHO LE-HAYBATEHI, \nO He before Whose Awe all faces have humbled themselves,\nوَ خَضَعَتِ الرِّقَابُ لِعَظَمَتِهٖ\nWA KHAZA-A’TIR REQAABO LE-A’ZAMATEHI,\nto His greatness all necks bend,\nوَ وَجِلَتِ الْقُلُوْبُ مِنْ خِيْفَتِهٖ\nWA WAJELATIL QOLOOBO MIN KHEEFATEHI \nand His fear makes the hearts quake!\nاَسْاَلُكَ بِهٰذِهِ الْمِدْحَةِ الَّتِىْ لَا تَنْبَغِيْ اِلَّا لَكَ\nAS-ALOKA BEHAAZEIL MIDHATIL LATEE LAA TAMBAGHEE ILLAA LAKA \nI beseech You in the name of this piece of praise which suits none but You,\nوَ بِمَا وَاَيْتَ بِهٖ عَلٰى نَفْسِكَ\nWA BEMAA WA AYTA BEHI A’LAA NAFSEKA \nand by the promise which You have made incumbent upon Yourself \nلِدَاعِيْكَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ\nLE-DAA-E’EKA MENAL MOAMENEENA \nfor the believers who call upon You,\nوَ بِمَا ضَمِنْتَ الْاِجَابَةَ فِيْهِ عَلٰى نَفْسِكَ لِلدَّاعِيْنَ\nWA BEMAA ZAMINTAL EJAABATA FEEHE A’LAA NAFSEKA LID-DAA-E’ENA \nand by the assurance You have given to answer the appeals of those who supplicate to You.\nيَا اَسْمَعَ السَّامِعِيْنَ\nYAA ASMA-A’S SAME-E’ENA, \nO the sharpest of listeners!\nوَ اَبْصَرَ النَّاظِرِيْنَ\nWA ABSARAN NAAZEREENA, \nand the keenest of observers!\nوَ اَسْرَعَ الْحَاسِبِيْنَ\nWA ASRA-A’L HAASEBEENA,\nand the swiftest of reckoners! \nيَا ذَا الْقُوَّةِ الْمَتِيْنَ\nYAA ZAL QUWWATIL MATEENA \nO Powerful and All-strong!\nصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ خَاتَمِ النَّبِيِّيْنَ\nSALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADIN KHAATAMIN NABIYYEENA \nbless Muhammad, the seal of the Prophets, \nوَ عَلٰى اَهْلِ بَيْتِهٖ\nWA A’LAA AHLE BAYTEHI \nand his Household,\nوَ اقْسِمْ لِيْ فِیْ شَهْرِنَا هٰذَا خَيْرَ مَا قَسَمْتَ\nWAQ SIM LEE FEE SHAHRENAA HAAZAA KHAYRA MAA QASAMTA \nand allot for me in this month of ours the best of what You have allotted to anyone,\nوَ احْتِمْ لِيْ فِیْ قَضَاۤئِكَ خَيْرَ مَا حَتَمْتَ\nWAH TIM LEE FEE QAZAAEKA KHAYRA MAA HATAMTA, \nand ordain for me in Your ordainments the best of what You have ordained for anyone,\nوَ اخْتِمْ لِیْ بِالسَّعَادَةِ فِيْمَنْ خَتَمْتَ\nWAKH TIM LEE BIS-SA-A’ADATE FEEMAN KHATAMTA \nseal my life with happiness with which You seal the lives of others,\nوَ اَحْيِنِيْ مَا اَحْيَيْتَنِيْ مَوْفُوْرًا\nWA AHYENEE MAA AHYAYTANEE MAWFOORAN \nGive me a prosperous life, so long as You keep me alive,\nوَ اَمِتْنِيْ مَسْرُوْرًا وَ مَغْفُوْرًا\nWA AMITNEE MASROORAN WA MAGHFOORAN \nand grant me to die happy and forgiven,\nوَ تَوَلَّ اَنْتَ نَجَاتِیْ مِنْ مُسَائَلَةِ الْبَرْزَخِ\nWA TAWALLA ANTA NAJAATEE MIN MOSAA-ALATIL BARZAKHE \nYou assume the charge of my deliverance during the questioning in the purgatory,\nوَ ادْرَاْ عَنِّیْ مُنْكَرًا وَ نَكِيْرًا\nWADRAA A’NNEE MUNKARAN WA NAKEERAN, \nand spare me from Munkar and Nakir,\nوَ اَرِ عَيْنِيْ مُبَشِّرًا وَّ بَشِيْرًا\nWA ARE A’YNEE MOBASHSHERANW WA BASHEERANW,\nand make Mubashshir and Bashir appear before my eyes,\nوَّ اجْعَلْ لِيْ اِلٰى رِضْوَانِكَ وَ جِنَانِكَ مَصِيْرًا\nWAJ A’L LEE ELAA RIZWAANEKA WA JENAANEKA MASEERAN\nlet my return be toward Your pleasure and paradise,\nوَ عَيْشًا قَرِيْرًا\nWA A’YSHAN QAREERAN, \nand grant me a happy life,\nوَ مُلْكًا كَبِيْرًا\nWA MULKAN KABEERAN,\nand a big kingdom, \nوَ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَ اٰلِهٖ كَثِيْرًا\nWA SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADINW WA AALEHI KASEERAA.\nand bless Muhammad and his Household very much.\nThis supplicatory prayer is also advisably said in Masjid Sa’sa’ah.\nFifth: Shaykh al-Tusi has narrated that the following holy Signature of Imam al-Mahdi(a.s.) was conveyed to the grand Shaykh Abu-Ja’far Muhammad ibn ‘Uthman ibn Sa’id:\nOn each day in Rajab, you may say the following supplicatory prayer:\nبِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMILLAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM. \nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّىْ اَسْاَلُكَ بِمَعَانِىْ جَمِيْعِ مَا يَدْعُوْكَ بِهٖ وُلَاةُ اَمْرِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE ASALOKA BE-MA-A’ANEE JAMEE-E’ MAA YADO’OKA BEHI WOLAATO AMREKAL \nO Allah, I beseech You by the meanings of all the supplications of those whom You have invested with Your authority,\nالْمَاْمُوْنُوْنَ عَلٰى سِرِّكَ\nMAAMOONOONA A’LAA SIRREKAL \nthe trustees of Your secret,\nالْمُسْتَبْشِرُوْنَ بِاَمْرِكَ\nMUSTABSHEROONA BE-AMREKAL, \nthose who rejoice in Your command,\nالْوَاصِفُوْنَ لِقُدْرَتِكَ\nWAASEFOONA LEQUDRATEKAL, \nthe describers of Your power,\nالْمُعْلِنُوْنَ لِعَظَمَتِكَ\nMO’LENOONA LE-A’ZAMATEKA, \nthe proclaimers of Your supremacy.\nاَسْاَلُكَ بِمَا نَطَقَ فِيْهِمْ مِنْ مَشِيَّتِكَ\nASALOKA BEMAA NATAQA HEEHIM MIM MASHIYYATEKA\nI implore You by Your will that has manifested itself through them\nفَجَعَلْتَهُمْ مَعَادِنَ لِكَلِمَاتِكَ\nFA-JA’ALTAHUM MA-A’ADENA LEKALEMAATEKA \nand thus You have made them the essences of Your Words,\nوَ اَرْكَانًا لِتَوْحِيْدِكَ\nWA ARKAANAN LE-TAWHEEDAKA \nthe pillars of Your Oneness,\nوَ آيَاتِكَ وَ مَقَامَاتِكَ الَّتِيْ لَا تَعْطِيْلَ لَهَا فِىْ كُلِّ مَكَانٍ\nWA AAYAATEKA WA MAQAAMAATEKAL LATEE LAA TA’TEELA LAHAA FEE KULLE MAKAANIN \nYour Signs and Stations, which are never inoperative in any place.\nيَعْرِفُكَ بِهَا مَنْ عَرَفَكَ\nYA’REFOKA BEHAA MAN A’RAFAKA, \nThrough them, You are known to those who know You.\nلَا فَرْقَ بَيْنَكَ وَ بَيْنَهَا اِلَّا اَنَّهُمْ عِبَادُكَ وَ خَلْقُكَ\nLAA FARQA BAYNAKA WA BAYNAHAA ILLAA ANNAHUM E’BAADOKA WA KHALQOKA, \n-there being no difference between You and them except that they are Your servants and creation.\nفَتْقُهَا وَ رَتْقُهَا بِيَدِكَ\nFATQOHAA WA RATQOHAA BEYADEKA, \ntheir unstitching and mending is in Your hand\nبَدْؤُهَا مِنْكَ وَ عَوْدُهَا اِلَيْكَ\nBAD-OHAA MINKA WA A’WDOHAA ELAYKA, \nthey enamate from You and return to You.\nاَعْضَادٌ وَ اَشْهَادٌ\nA-A’ZAADUN WA ASH-HAADUN \nThey are the instruments, witnesses,\nوَ مُنَاةٌ وَ اَذْوَادٌ\nWA MONAATUN WA AZWAADUN \nplanners, defenders\nوَ حَفَظَةٌ وَ رُوَّادٌ\nWA HAFAZATUN WA RUWWAADUN,\nguards and scouts\nفَبِهِمْ مَلَأْتَ سَمَائَكَ وَ اَرْضَكَ\nFABEHIM MALAATA SAMAA-AKA WA ARZAKA \nby whose means You have filled Your heavens and earth\nحَتّٰى ظَهَرَ اَنْ لَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ\nHATTAA ZAHARA AN LAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANTA, \nuntil it became manifest that there is no god save You.\nفَبِذٰلِكَ اَسْاَلُكَ\nFA-BEZAALEKA AS-ALOKA \nI thus implore You in the name of all this,\nوَ بِمَوَاقِعِ الْعِزِّ مِنْ رَّحْمَتِكَ\nWA BE-MAWAA-QE-I’L I’ZZE MIR RAHMATEKA \nand by the recipients of honor and might by your mercy,\nوَ بِمَقَامَاتِكَ وَ عَلَامَاتِكَ\nWA BE-MAQAAMAATEKA WA A’LAAMAATEKA, \nand by Your stations and Signs,\nاَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَ اٰلِهٖ\nAN TOSALLEYA A’LAA MOHAMMADINW WA AALEHI \nto send blessings to Muhammad and his Household\nوَ اَنْ تَزِيْدَنِيْ اِيْمَانًا وَ تَثْبِيْتًا\nWA AN TAZEEDANEE EEMAANAN WA TASBEETAN \nand increase me in faith and fortitude.\nيَا بَاطِنًا فِي ظُهُوْرِهٖ\nYAA BAATENAN FEE ZOHOOREHI \nO He Who is Immanent in His Evidence!\nوَ ظَاهِرًا فِي بُطُوْنِهٖ وَ مَكْنُوْنِهٖ\nWA ZAAHERAN FEE BOTOONEHI WA MAKNOONEHI \nO He Who is Evident in His Immanence and in His hiddenness!\nيَا مُفَرِّقًا بَيْنَ النُّوْرِ وَ الدَّيْجُوْرِ\nYAA MOFARREQAN BAYNAN NOORE WAD-DAYJOORE \nO He Who sets apart light from murk!\nيَا مَوْصُوْفًا بِغَيْرِ كُنْهٍ\nYAA MAWSOOFAN BE-GHAYRE KUNHIN, \nO He Whom is described without recognition of his real essence!\nوَ مَعْرُوْفًا بِغَيْرِ شِبْهٍ\nWA MA’ROOFAN BE-GHAYRE SHIBHIN, \nand He Whom is recognized without having anything like Him!\nحَادَّ كُلِّ مَحْدُوْدٍ\nHAADDA KULLE MAHDOODIN, \nO Edger of all edged things!\nوَ شَاهِدَ كُلِّ مَشْهُوْدٍ\nWA SHAAHEDA KULLE MASH-HOODIN\nO Witness of all done things!\nوَ مُوْجِدَ كُلِّ مَوْجُودٍ\nWA MOOJEDA KLLE MAWJOODIN \nO Bringer into being all existent things!\nوَ مُحْصِيَ كُلِّ مَعْدُوْدٍ\nWA MOHSEYA KULLE MA’DOODIN \nO Knower of the number of all countable things!\nوَ فَاقِدَ كُلِّ مَفْقُودٍ،\nWA FAAQEDA KULLE MAFQOODIN \nO Knower of the place of all lost things!\nلَيْسَ دُوْنَكَ مِنْ مَعْبُوْدٍ\nLAYSA DOONAKA MIM MA’BOODIN, \nNone is worshipped except You.\nاَهْلَ الْكِبْرِيَاءِ وَ الْجُوْدِ\nAHLAL KIBREYAA-E WAL-JOODE, \nYou are the worthiest of all pride and magnanimity.\nيَا مَنْ لَا يُكَيَّفُ بِكَيْفٍ\nYAA MAN LAA YOKAYYAFO BE-KAYFIN, \nO He about Whom, it is infeasible to as ‘how’\nوَ لَا يُؤَيَّنُ بِاَيْنٍ\nWA LAA YO-AYYANO BE-AYNIN, \nand it is infeasible to ask ‘where’!\nيَا مُحْتَجِبًا عَنْ كُلِّ عَيْنٍ\nYAA MOHTAJEBAN A’N KULLE A’YNIN, \nO He Who is concealed from all sights!\nيَا دَيْمُوْمُ يَا قَيُّوْمُ وَ عَالِمَ كُلِّ مَعْلُوْمٍ\nYAA DAYMOOMO YAA QAYYOOMO WA A’ALEMA KULLE MA’LOOMIN, \nO Everlasting, O Self-Subsistent, O Knower of all known things!\nصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَ اٰلِهٖ وَ عَلٰى عِبَادِكَ الْمُنْتَجَبِيْنَ\nSALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADINW WA AALEHI WA A’LAA E’BAADEKAL MUNTAJABEENA \nsend blessings to Muhammad, his Household, Your selected servants,\nوَ بَشَرِكَ الْمُحْتَجِبِيْنَ\nWA BASHAREKAL MOHTAJEBEENA, \nYour concealed human beings,\nوَ مَلَاۤئِكَتِكَ الْمُقَرَّبِيْنَ\nWA MA-LAA-EKATEKAL MOQARRABEENA \nYour favorite angels,\nوَ الْبُهْمِ الصَّافِّيْنَ الْحَافِّيْنَ\nWAL-BOHMIS SAAF-FEENAL HAAFFEENA \nand the Angels who draw themselves out in ranks and who throng (round the Divine Throne),\nوَ بَارِكْ لَنَا فِي شَهْرِنَا هٰذَا الْمُرَجَّبِ الْمُكَرَّمِ\nWA BAARIK LANAA FEE SHAHRENAA HAAZAL MORAJJABIL MOKARRAME \nand bless us in this month—the honored and dignified—\nوَ مَا بَعْدَهٗ مِنَ الْاَشْهُرِ الْحُرُمِ\nWA MAA BA’DAHU MENAL ASH-HORIL HOROME \nas well as the next sacred months,\nوَ اَسْبِغْ عَلَيْنَا فِيْهِ النِّعَمَ\nWA ASBIGH A’LAYNAA FEEHIN NE-A’MA \npour upon us Your graces in this month,\nوَ اَجْزِلْ لَنَا فِيْهِ الْقِسَمَ\nWA AJ-ZIL LANAA FEEHIL QESAMA \ngrant us abundant shares of blessings,\nوَ اَبْرِرْ لَنَا فِيْهِ الْقَسَمَ\nWA ABRIR LANAA FEEHIL QASAMA \nadmit our requests,\nبِاسْمِكَ الْاَعْظَمِ الْاَعْظَمِ الْاَجَلِّ الْاََكْرَمِ\nBISMEKAL A-A’ZAMIL A-A’ZAMIL AJALLIL AKRAMIL \nin the name of Your Name, the Greatest, the Greatest, the Loftiest, the Most Honored\nالَّذِيْ وَضَعْتَهُ عَلَى النَّهَارِ فَاَضَاءَ\nLAZEE WA ZA’TAHU A’LAN NAHAARE FA-AZAA-A \nthat You put on daylight and it thus lit up\nوَ عَلَى اللَّيْلِ فَاَظْلَمَ\nWA A’LAL LAYLE FA-AZLAMA \nand You put on night and it thus darkened,\nوَ اغْفِرْ لَنَا مَا تَعْلَمُ مِنَّا وَ مَا لَا نَعْلَمُ\nWAGH FIR LANAA MAA TA’LAMO MINNAA WA MAA LAA NA’LAMO, \nforgive us all that which You know about us and all that which we do not know,\nوَ اعْصِمْنَا مِنَ الذُّنُوْبِ خَيْرَ الْعِصَمِ\nWA’ SIMNAA MENAZ ZONOOBE KHAYRAL E’SAME, \nprotect us against sins with the best of protection,\nوَ اكْفِنَا كَوَافِيَ قَدَرِكَ\nWAK FENAA KAWAAFEYA QADAREKA, \nsave us against the acts that You predetermine,\nوَ امْنُنْ عَلَيْنَا بِحُسْنِ نَظَرِكَ\nWAM NUN A’LAYNAA BEHUSNE NAZAREKA, \nbestow upon us with Your superb looking,\nوَ لَا تَكِلْنَا اِلٰى غَيْرِكَ\nWA LAA TAKILNAA ELAA GHAYREKA, \ndo not leave us in the hands of anyone other than You,\nوَ لَا تَمْنَعْنَا مِنْ خَيْرِكَ\nWA LAA TAM-NA’NAA MIN KHAYREKA, \ndo not prevent us from Your goodness,\nوَ بَارِكْ لَنَا فِيْمَا كَتَبْتَهُ لَنَا مِنْ اَعْمَارِنَا\nWA BAARIK LANAA FEEMAA KATABTAHU LANAA MIN A-A’MAARENAA, \nbless us during the age that You have decided for us,\nوَ اَصْلِحْ لَنَا خَبِيْئَةَ اَسْرَارِنَا\nWA ASLEH LANAA KHABEE-ATA ASRAARENAA \nmake righteous for us our inner selves,\nوَ اَعْطِنَا مِنْكَ الْاَمَانَ\nWA A-A’TENAA MINKAL AMAANA, \ngrant us Your security,\nوَ اسْتَعْمِلْنَا بِحُسْنِ الْاِيمَانِ\nWAS TA’MILNAA BE-HUSNIL EEMAANE,\nmake us enjoy perfect faith,\nوَ بَلِّغْنَا شَهْرَ الصِّيَامِ\nWA BALLIGHNAA SHAHRAS SEYAAME, \nand make us catch the month of fasting\nوَ مَا بَعْدَهٗ مِنَ الْاَيَّامِ وَ الْاَعْوَامِ\nWA MAA BA’DAHU MENAL AYYAAME WAL A-A’WAAME, \nand the days and years coming after,\nيَا ذَا الْجَلَالِ وَ الْاِكْرَامِ.\nYAA ZAL JALAALE WAL IKRAAME.\nO Lord of Majesty and Honor!\nSixth: Shaykh al-Tusi has also narrated that a document signed by Imam al-Mahdi (a.t.f.s.) was received by Shaykh Abul Qasim, Imam al-Mahdi (a.t.f.s.)’s representative, comprising that the following supplicatory prayer would be recommendably said in the month of Rajab:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْ اَسْاَلُكَ بِالْمَوْلُوْدَيْنِ فِي رَجَبٍ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOKA BIL-MAWLOODAYNE FEE RAJABIN\nO Allah, I beseech You in the name of those who were born in Rajab, \nمُحَمَّدِ بْنِ عَلِيٍّ۟ الثَّانِىْ\nMOHAMMAD IBNE A’LIYYENIS SAANEE \nMuhammad ibn Ali the second\nوَ ابْنِهٖ عَلِيِّ بْنِ مُحَمَّدٍۨ الْمُنْتَجَبِ\nWAB NEHI A’LIYYIBNE MOHAMMADENIL MUNTAJABE \nand his son Ali ibn Muhammad the divinely selected;\nوَ اَتَقَرَّبُ بِهِمَا اِلَيْكَ خَيْرَ الْقُرَبِ\nWA ATAQARRABO BEHEMAA ELAYKA KHAYRAL QORABE \nI seek nearness to You through both of them for they are the best means of nearness to You.\nيَا مَنْ اِلَيْهِ الْمَعْرُوْفُ طُلِبَ\nYAA MAN ELAYHIL MA’ROOFO TOLEBA \nO He from Whom favors are sought\nوَ فِيْمَا لَدَيْهِ رُغِبَ\nWA FEEMAA LADAYHE ROGHEBA \nand what He possesses is desired!\nاَسْاَلُكَ سُؤَالَ مُقْتَرِفٍ مُذْنِبٍ\nAS-ALOKA SO-AALA MUQTAREFIN MUZNEBIN \nI beseech You with the entreaty of him\nقَدْ اَوْبَقَتْهُ ذُنُوْبُهٗ\nQAD AW BAQATHO ZONOOBOHU\nwhom is enchained by his sins\nوَ اَوْثَقَتْهُ عُيُوْبُهٗ\nWA AW SAQATHO O’YOOBOHU\nand is bound by his defects;\nفَطَالَ عَلَى الْخَطَايَا دُئُوْبُهٗ\nFA-TAALA A’LAL KHATAAYAA DO-OOBOHU \ntherefore, he devoted himself to offenses,\nوَ مِنَ الرَّزَايَا خُطُوْبُهٗ\nWA MENAR RAZAAYAA KHOTOOBOHU\nand disasters have attacked him heavily.\nيَسْاَلُكَ التَّوْبَةَ\nYASALOKAT TAWBATA \nHe is now begging You for accepting his repentance,\nوَ حُسْنَ الْاَوْبَةِ\nWA HUSNAL AWBATE \ngood return from You,\nوَ النُّزُوْعَ عَنِ الْحَوْبَةِ\nWAN-NOZOO-A A’NIL HAWBATE\nredeeming from punishment,\nوَ مِنَ النَّارِ فَكَاكَ رَقَبَتِهٖ\nWA MENAN NAARE FAKAAKA RAQABATEHI \nreleasing from Hellfire,\nوَ الْعَفْوَ عَمَّا فِیْ رِبْقَتِهٖ\nWAL A’FWA A’MMAA FEE RIBQATEHI \nand overlooking the sins that are hanged to him.\nفَاَنْتَ مَوْلَايَ اَعْظَمُ اَمَلِهٖ وَ ثِقَتِهٖ\nFA-ANTA MAWLAAYA A-A’ZAMO AMALEHI WA SEQATEHI.\nCertainly, You, O my Master, the greatest of all hopes and desires he has.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ وَ اَسْاَلُكَ بِمَسَاۤئِلِكَ الشَّرِيْفَةِ\nALLAAHUMMA WA AS-ALOKA BE-MASAAA-ELEKASH SHAREEFATE \nO Allah, I beg You in the name of the holy means that You admit\nوَ وَسَاۤئِلِكَ الْمُنِيْفَةِ\nWA WASAAA-ELEKAL MONEEFATE \nand all of the elevated courses that take to You\nاَنْ تَتَغَمَّدَنِیْ فِیْ هٰذَا الشَّهْرِ بِرَحْمَةٍ مِنْكَ وَاسِعَةٍ\nAN TATAGHAMMADANEE FEE HAAZASH SHAHRE BE-RAHMATIM MINKA WAASE-A’TIN \nto encompass me, in this month, with vast mercy of You, \nوَ نِعْمَةٍ وَازِعَةٍ\nWA NE’MATIN WAAZE-A’TIN \nabundant favors,\nوَ نَفْسٍ بِمَا رَزَقْتَهَا قَانِعَةٍ\nWA NAFSIM BEMAA RAZAQTAHAA QAANEA’TIN \nand satisfaction with what You have decided for me\nاِلٰى نُزُوْلِ الْحَافِرَةِ\nELAA NOZOOLIL HAAFERATE \nuntil I am put in my final hole,\nوَ مَحَلِّ الْآخِرَةِ\nWA MAHALLIL AAKHERATE \nwhich is my abode to the Hereafter\nوَ مَا هِيَ اِلَيْهِ صَاۤئِرَةٌ.\nWA MAA HEYA ELAYHE SAA-ERATUN.\nand the Final Fate."
}
